    "explanation": "This is the decision on TRP-05055, addressed to both parties. The rider booked a scheduled 07:30 pickup. Under POL-NS-24 the driver had to reach the pickup by 07:35 (07:30 plus 5 minutes). Two independent records, each at full weight (1.0), show he did not. The platform trip record records no arrival (arrived_at null; derived driver_deadline.arrived_by_deadline false against a deadline of 07:35:00 and driver_late_after_scheduled_sec 300). The driver-device GPS trace - complete, 50 fixes, 100% coverage, no gap above 30 s - puts the vehicle stationary roughly 1.1 km from the pickup from 07:33:10 until the 07:37:40 cancellation, with no fix inside the 50 m arrival radius (arrival_check.corroborated false, nearest_fix null). Because the driver did not arrive by the deadline, POL-NS-24 gives the rider the right to cancel at no charge and any fee charged is refunded in full. The 5.00 SGD cancellation fee charged at 07:37:44 (EV-FARE-05055; total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is therefore refunded in full: FULL_REFUND of 5.00 SGD, with driver_compensation_sgd null. For the driver: the points in your favour are accepted but do not change the result. You did discharge POL-NS-23's contact obligation - your message at 07:31:10 and your answered 40-second in-app call at 07:33:20 both precede the 07:37:40 cancellation - so the fee is not voided on the contact ground; but meeting the contact obligation does not excuse the separate failure to arrive that POL-NS-24 addresses. The 5.00 SGD charged is the correct POL-NS-22 amount and the ledger reconciles, but a correct amount does not make payable a fee that POL-NS-24 requires be refunded. The Sembawang Road congestion you report, and the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05055-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT, carrying no fact either way), do not supply a traffic exception: POL-NS-24 contains none. No further adjustment follows. The driver did attempt contact, so POL-NS-24's 5.00 SGD goodwill credit does not arise; the rider profile does not carry no_show_cancellations_30d, so POL-NS-25's repeat no-show referral does not fire; the fee is exactly 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not fire. There is no safety flag and the value (5.00 SGD) is below 10.00 SGD, so the AI ruling is final and no escalation applies. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.0 POL-NS-26 requires for a no-show of this value; the deciding fact is carried by two independent artifacts, the trip record and the GPS trace, both at weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"FULL_REFUND","amount_sgd":5.00,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"Rider: your cancellation is upheld and the 5.00 SGD fee is returned in full. Your trip was scheduled for 07:30 (EV-TRIP-05055). Under POL-NS-21 the driver held a 5-minute free wait, so he was required at the pickup by 07:35:00, and POL-NS-24 gives you the right to cancel at no charge if he had not arrived by then, with any fee charged refunded in full. The record shows he had not: the trip record carries arrived_at null and its derived driver_deadline returns arrived_by_deadline false against the 07:35:00 deadline (EV-TRIP-05055), and the complete 50-fix driver trace (EV-GPS-05055, 100% coverage, maximum interval 30 s, no gaps) never places the vehicle within the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (POL-NS-21) — its last fixes show the car stationary roughly a kilometre from the pickup from 07:33:10 until your 07:37:40 cancellation. You cancelled at 07:37:40, after the deadline the driver missed, so the 5.00 SGD charged at 07:37:44 (EV-FARE-05055) is refunded in full under POL-GEN-03.

Driver: your account of the Sembawang Road jam is considered, and your trace's very low reported speeds are consistent with congestion, but POL-NS-24 contains no traffic exception, and the traffic advisory you would rely on (EV-ADVIS-05055-01) is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so under POL-GEN-02(3) it carries no fact. You did satisfy POL-NS-23's contact obligation — your 07:31:10 in-app message and the answered 40-second call placed at 07:33:20 both precede the cancellation (EV-CHAT-05055, EV-TRIP-05055) — so the fee is not voided on the contact ground, and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit under POL-NS-24 arises, because that credit requires a failure to attempt contact, which the record disproves. Your POL-NS-22 point that the ledger charges exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee is accurate but does not preserve it: POL-NS-22 authorises the no-show fee where the driver cancels after the free wait, and here the rider cancelled, so the fee falls to be refunded under POL-NS-24 rather than upheld. POL-GEN-26 does not require escalation: the fact POL-NS-24 turns on — whether the driver arrived by 07:35 — is answered by the trip record and the complete trace, and the only missing artifact carries no fact for either side.

No referral arises. The POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not fire (contact was attempted); the POL-NS-22 fee-amount check does not fire (the fee is exactly 5.00 SGD); and the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show flag does not fire (the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter and this fee does not stand)."},"discarded_claims":[]}
